From: Peios maintainers <packaging@peios.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: use a typed load-module setup prototype

C23 no longer treats an empty parameter list as an unspecified parameter
list.  Give the generated loadable-module test the prototype implemented
later in the same source so current compilers can build and exercise it.

Peios's GCC defaults to C23 and runs Make's test suite as a build gate, so
without this the loadapi test fails to compile and the load API goes
untested. Only the test changes; make itself is unchanged.

Current GNU Make development sources also use a typed prototype, with the
newer load-module ABI.  This is the corresponding fix for the 4.4.1 ABI,
so there is nothing to forward.

Forwarded: not-needed
---
 tests/scripts/features/loadapi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/scripts/features/loadapi b/tests/scripts/features/loadapi
index d42ec97..8a91745 100644
--- a/tests/scripts/features/loadapi
+++ b/tests/scripts/features/loadapi
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ char *getenv (const char*);
 
 int plugin_is_GPL_compatible;
 
-int testapi_gmk_setup ();
+int testapi_gmk_setup (const gmk_floc *);
 
 static char *
 test_eval (const char *buf)
